       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose, a 70 kg adult could develop severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. The effects can last a long time because amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nCould you check whether one of these applies?\n- **Typo:** you may have meant 5 mg, which is a common starting dose, or 10 mg, which is the maximum.\n- **Different drug or formulation:** you may have meant another medication.\n- **Intentional dose:** if you really want 50 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. For example, \"5 mg PO once daily\" would be a standard order."
